# Mobile calculator shell

Below Tailwind `lg` (1024px) the calculator uses a single-column chrome from
the v2 mobile mockup. Desktop (`lg+`) stays the two-column sidebar + results
layout. Same route: `useLgUp()` picks one tree after the first client measure
so the desktop sidebar is not a `display: none` node on phones. The root
`viewport` export locks scale (`maximum-scale=1`, `user-scalable=no`) so the
tool does not pinch-zoom.

## Layout (below `lg`)

```
TopBar (compact: logo, Roth Calculator, hamburger)
DeviceNotice (one-time fullscreen modal; localStorage
  rothCalcBestViewedModalSeen)
main (overflow-y scroller for pin-to-top)
  MobileResultsChrome (plan name + switch button, status; Plan details modal)
  ResultsView (unchanged)
MobileActionBar (Configure, Details, Actions. Details opens the plan modal)
```

The chrome Footer is omitted below `lg` so it does not sit under the sticky
bar. It stays **outside** `<main>` on desktop (pin-to-top contract). Do not
move Footer into the results scroller.

## Shared pieces (do not duplicate)

| Piece | Used by |
| ---- | ---- |
| `PlanPicker` | Desktop TopBar, mobile Plan details modal. Names ascending, with a search field |
| `PlanActions` | Sidebar header, `MobileActionBar` (bar: Configure / Details / Actions) |
| `PlanDetails` | Sidebar, mobile Plan details modal |
| `PlanStatus` | Sidebar card, mobile page banner |
| `StrategyPanel` | Sidebar, mobile Plan details modal |
| `usePlanAccess` | Permissions for the above |

`ConversionStrategyMenu` is not in the mockup. On mobile it lives in the Plan
details modal, under the plan picker (same modal as the timeline/summary).
The page title is the plan name plus a circular switch-plan button; tap
either to open Plan details (same as the sticky Details button). Do not
auto-open Plan details.
Switching plan, New plan, changing strategy, or Edit closes the modal via
`closePlanDetails` in `useUI`. Do not put the plan picker in a second
sticky header bar.

## Gotchas

- Wait for `useLgUp().ready` before painting the calculator, or mobile flashes
  the desktop sidebar for a frame. `lgUp` is false during SSR/hydrate so the
  desktop Footer is not in the HTML (it would otherwise appear, then vanish
  on the phone).
- A Next.js hydration warning that only mentions `data-cursor-ref` is the
  Cursor browser tagging the DOM before React hydrates, not an app mismatch.
- Projection table pin-to-top still needs `<main>` as the nearest
  `overflow-y` parent. Pad `<main>` so the sticky bar does not cover content;
  do not wrap the table in a max-height card. Keep `min-w-0` / `w-full` on
  the results column so the wide table does not stretch metric cards past
  the viewport. Below `lg`, each metric card is one full-width column.
  The year-by-year sticky label column is `w-36` with wrapping `text-sm`
  below `lg` (desktop stays `15rem` nowrap) so long names do not eat the
  year columns. Section titles stay one line (`nowrap`); only data-row
  names wrap. Section titles are one `colSpan` cell with full-width
  `bg-accent-soft` so a stuck title covers the previous one. The title
  text uses `left-2` / `lg:left-3` (not `left-0`) so it keeps the same
  inset when it sticks. Year cells stay `z-20` so they slide under the
  left corner (`z-30`) and clip at the label column. Section bars are
  `z-10` under the years. `top` is the measured year-header height minus
  3px, plus a 3px white strip (`box-shadow`, because collapsed table
  borders do not paint).
- Wizard, charts, and table behavior are out of scope for this shell.
- `DeviceNotice` is a one-time fullscreen overlay (not a banner). It only
  mounts on the mobile tree and writes `rothCalcBestViewedModalSeen`. Clear
  that key to see it again.
- The Feedback FAB is desktop only (`lg+`). Below `lg` it is hidden; signed-in
  users open the same form from Feedback in the hamburger menu.
- Signed-in account menus (hamburger below `lg`, name/email menu on `lg+`)
  share one order: user + email, divider, Feedback, divider, View as user
  (superAdmin only), Sign out. View as user and Sign out have icons.
- Plan Actions includes **Download JSON** for the real superAdmin only
  (`session.user.superAdmin` or `session.impersonation.active`: the flag is
  stripped while viewing as another user). It downloads the in-memory plan
  (`exportConfig`), including unsaved edits and a revision preview.
- Save toasts (`ToastHost`) sit top-center below `lg`
  (`top-[calc(0.75rem+env(safe-area-inset-top))]`). Desktop stays top-right.
